LISA atomic_of_block_scope_across_blocks
(* An atomic of block scope does not synchronize with a lane of another block (C7). The flag
   does not publish the data, and the threads race. This is why the scope of an atomic must come
   from its memory space, and not from the programmer.
   Expect: sometimes, a data race. *)
{ data = 0; flag = 0; }
 P0                     | P1                     ;
 w[plain] data 1        | r[acq,block] r0 flag   ;
 w[rel,block] flag 1    | r[plain] r1 data       ;
scopes: (device (block P0) (block P1))
filter (1:r0 = 1)
exists (1:r1 = 0)
